WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.903
Live support provides situational awareness without taking command from the pilot.

00:00:05.903 --> 00:00:15.584
The center may track mission status, crew check-ins, weather, airspace changes, telemetry summaries, communications, data milestones, and outstanding hazards.

00:00:15.584 --> 00:00:26.682
Status boards should show what requires action: mission phase, crew, aircraft, location, communication state, battery or timing milestones, warnings, and escalation status.

00:00:26.682 --> 00:00:32.585
Stale data must be marked clearly rather than presented as current.

00:00:32.585 --> 00:00:34.710
Communication discipline matters.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:43.918
Safety-critical messages receive priority, standard terms reduce ambiguity, and the center avoids flooding the pilot with nonessential requests.

00:00:43.918 --> 00:00:49.349
Payload or client questions wait when aircraft control requires attention.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:56.669
Emergency support can provide contacts, maps, weather, airspace information, coordination, and a decision log.

00:00:56.669 --> 00:01:05.405
The center should know when to contact emergency, aviation, site, security, or management authorities under approved procedures.

00:01:05.405 --> 00:01:11.781
Abort criteria belong to the plan and are monitored during the mission.

00:01:11.781 --> 00:01:22.878
Weather, aircraft warnings, battery anomalies, signal degradation, people entering the area, privacy concerns, or loss of authorization may require return or landing.

00:01:22.878 --> 00:01:28.309
Handoffs preserve authority and context when shifts or teams change.

00:01:28.309 --> 00:01:35.629
After landing, an after-action review captures deviations, decisions, equipment issues, data quality, and lessons.

00:01:35.629 --> 00:01:42.476
Live support adds value when it reduces pilot workload and improves organizational learning.

00:01:42.476 --> 00:01:47.907
When several missions are active, the center must prioritize attention.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:55.699
High-risk phases, emergency calls, lost communication, and deteriorating conditions take precedence over routine status updates.

00:01:55.699 --> 00:01:59.713
Staffing and displays should reflect that hierarchy.
